id: pm-gh1553
title: "GH-1553: investigate history union scalar replay refusal on concurrent appends"
description: "External report from pm-web using pm-cli 2026.10.19: history merge refuses scalar rebase when main closes an item and a branch appends comments/field edits. Reproduce on current SDK before changing the fail-closed replay contract; a manually unioned stream passing health alone is not proof that event semantics are lossless."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: context-management,"gh:1553",sdk
created_at: "2026-10-23T06:27:49.281Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-24T21:14:39.127Z"
assignee: "harness:codex"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#e495e5b5774b85b06e5f8657"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Current-version fixture reproduces or disproves the reported event sequence; Each scalar transition and retained event is checked against strict replay; Any safe correction preserves hash/replay integrity and provides actionable refusal evidence.
parent: pm-o2kc
risk: medium
confidence: medium
expected_result: A current-version fixture establishes scalar replay semantics for the reported merge before any correction; safe unions retain every event and unsafe transitions refuse with actionable coordinates.
